# UI snappiness performance log (2026-11-12)

## Baseline (Node, main before changes)

| Scenario | p50 | p95 | max |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| ai-vs-ai-lab ×100 | 268 ms | 505 ms | 651 ms |
| ai-vs-ai-skirmish ×100 | 744 ms | 1292 ms | 1709 ms |
| continents CvC ×60 | 252 ms | 365 ms | 391 ms |

Skirmish mid-game (~18 units): ~670 ms/round with ~1545 `structuredClone` calls.

## After PR1+PR2 engine/UI work

| Scenario | p50 | p95 | max |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| ai-vs-ai-lab ×100 | 127 ms | 231 ms | 300 ms |
| ai-vs-ai-skirmish ×100 | 391 ms | 616 ms | 764 ms |
| continents CvC ×60 | 119 ms | 153 ms | 169 ms |

Roughly **2×** faster AI rounds. Skirmish p95 still above a soft 400 ms goal.

## Changes shipped on `perf/ui-snappiness`

1. **UI:** rAF-coalesced pan/zoom paint; world terrain+fog layer cache; cheap CvC scorecards; skip inspector/events rebuild when unchanged.
2. **Engine:** one private clone per AI turn (`mutable` ops); reused `PlayerView` + unit/hostile-city indexes in `playAiOpponent`.
3. **Save/playback:** compact IndexedDB autosave with latest-wins coalescing; `labRoundPhases` yields between AI/endTurn phases; Pause finishes the open round onto a blue turn.
4. **Harness:** `scripts/bench-rounds.mjs`; tests `ai-mutable-turn`, `autosave-compact`.

## Map draw split terrain/fog (2026-11-13)

**Observation:** CvC observer rounds felt faster with opaque / reveal-off fog because
unexplored tiles were cheap solid fills instead of full atlas stamps under translucent fog.

**Baseline (Node, no browser — this machine cannot run Playwright):**

| Step | Cost |
|---|---:|
| `getPlayerView` after 10 CvC rounds | ~1.7 ms |
| Full-map terrain+fog lookups (6000 tiles) | ~0.3 ms |
| Full-map canvas atlas rebuild | Dominates flush paint (inferred; skipped locally) |

**Change:** Cache geography separately from fog. Reveal-on key is
`geo|tilesRevision|tileSize` (ignores knowledge generation). Fog always overlays in
`paintFrame`. `refresh()` only invalidates knowledge stamps when not CvC reveal-on.

**Verify:** `tests/observer-map.test.mjs` locally; `smoke/observer.mjs` / Playwright on GitHub Actions only.
